Cell["\<\
Figure 2.2  Phase diagram in \[Chi]\[Dash]\[Phi] coordinates. The blue curve \
is the binodal (coexistence); the red dashed curve is the spinodal (stability \
limit). Between them: metastable (nucleation and growth). Inside the \
spinodal: unstable (spinodal decomposition). The black dot is the critical \
point.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"4e4c8d48-4c62-49a3-aded-9a5ed9251c22"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2.3  Chain length and multivalency", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"01caf0a0-8ab0-420c-9b1a-4a153f773bf5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A key prediction of Flory\[Dash]Huggins theory is that ",
 StyleBox["longer polymers phase-separate more readily",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ". The critical interaction falls toward ",
 StyleBox["1/2",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " as chain length grows, with the excess ",
 StyleBox["\[Chi]\:1d9c - 1/2",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " scaling as ",
 StyleBox["N^(-1/2)",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ": a 1000-mer demixes at ",
 StyleBox["\[Chi]\:1d9c \[TildeTilde] 0.53",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " versus ",
 StyleBox["\[TildeTilde] 0.87",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " for a 10-mer, so long chains phase-separate at appreciably weaker \
interactions. This is biologically significant: intrinsically disordered \
regions (IDRs) of condensate-forming proteins are typically 50\[Dash]500 \
residues, and their effective ",
 StyleBox["N",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " is further increased by multivalent interactions (multiple binding sites \
per molecule, RNA scaffolds, post-translational modifications)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bab47f0e-1646-4c83-b872-42ce7fd90955"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"figFHChainLength", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
   "1", ",", " ", "5", ",", " ", "20", ",", " ", "100", ",", " ", "500"}], 
   "}"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->" In[8]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1c33252d-a062-42c6-9039-85df56409b07"],

