}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Figure 8.3  (a) Flory\[Dash]Huggins phase diagram: binodal (coexistence, \
blue) outside the spinodal (instability, red dashed), meeting at the critical \
point; the orange dot marks the solver operating point (\[Phi] = 0.3, \[Chi] \
= 1.5). (b) The symmetric double-well pitchfork, with the metastable region \
between binodal and spinodal.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"5dd1a5ea-7eea-43d2-a921-57e68e2b12e1"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["8.4  The free energy as a Lyapunov functional", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"ad16b892-a867-40ef-afa2-126bd9855ea2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Cahn\[Dash]Hilliard dynamics are a ",
 StyleBox["gradient flow",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " of the free-energy functional ",
 StyleBox["F[\[Phi]] = \[Integral] [ f(\[Phi]) + (\[Kappa]/2) |\[Del]\[Phi]|\
\.b2 ] dx",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ". Conservation of \[Phi] and the structure of the equation guarantee ",
 StyleBox["dF/dt \[LessEqual] 0",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ": F is a ",
 StyleBox["Lyapunov functional",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " and the phase-separated state is its minimiser. Each coarsening event \
\[LongDash] two domains merging \[LongDash] appears as a step down in F."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fb665ba9-69aa-4062-9a2d-24387864b207"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"figEnergyLyapunov", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  " In[23]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a51b7c2b-01c9-449b-8dce-c373862846fc"],

Cell[OutputFormData["\<\
-Graphics-\
\>"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9914751651533318`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  " Out[23]=",ExpressionUUID->"8da82cd3-4bde-4829-93b0-d0b59c5bdf64"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Figure 8.4  (a) Space\[Dash]time evolution of the 1D double-well \
Cahn\[Dash]Hilliard equation (NDSolve): domains form, then coarsen by \
merging. (b) The free energy F[\[Phi]] decreases monotonically, falling in \
discrete steps as domains coalesce \[LongDash] the signature of a Lyapunov \
functional. (Note: the strongly stabilised Flory\[Dash]Huggins solver instead \
freezes; the canonical t\[ThinSpace]^(1/3) coarsening, with ",
 StyleBox["L\.b3 = L\:2080\.b3 + K\[ThinSpace]t",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " linear in time, is reproduced by the double-well Model B in the Python \
implementation.)"
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"1673d507-b428-46aa-9d2c-538e0149646c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["8.5  Mass-conserving reaction enhancement", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"7d80f53f-8352-4cdd-9943-0804bb72e996"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Section 4 estimated the bimolecular rate boost inside a condensate as ",
 StyleBox["K_A K_B",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ". That is the ",
 StyleBox["open-system",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " limit (buffered reservoir). Imposing ",
 StyleBox["mass conservation",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " \[LongDash] the condensate concentrates reactants but ",
 StyleBox["depletes",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " the surrounding dilute phase \[LongDash] gives a very different answer. \
With dense area fraction ",
 StyleBox["p",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " and rapid partitioning ",
 StyleBox["c_in = K\[ThinSpace]c_out",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " in each phase, the volume-averaged rate relative to a well-mixed system \
is"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"51012ffe-1787-444d-a952-a642cc9d7ca2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    SubscriptBox["k", "eff"], 
    SubscriptBox["k", "out"]], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"p", " ", 
     SubscriptBox["K", "A"], 
     SubscriptBox["K", "B"], "+", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", "-", "p"}], ")"}]}], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", "+", 
       RowBox[{"p", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox["K", "A"], "-", "1"}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", "+", 
       RowBox[{"p", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox["K", "B"], "-", "1"}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}]}]]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellMargins->{{80, 50}, {8, 
  8}},ExpressionUUID->"486a0115-9e9d-4675-901d-3f43c1740fad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The enhancement vanishes at both ",
 StyleBox["p \[Rule] 0",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (no condensate) and ",
 StyleBox["p \[Rule] 1",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (everything uniform); it is maximal at an ",
 StyleBox["intermediate dense fraction",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " ",
 StyleBox["p* \[TildeTilde] 1/K",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", where the gain is only ",
 StyleBox["\[TildeTilde] K/4",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " \[LongDash] not the naive ",
 StyleBox["K\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ". Bulk depletion is the hard ceiling on condensate catalysis, and it \
predicts an optimal droplet volume fraction \[LongDash] a falsifiable, \
quantitative claim."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"858268b2-47f3-487a-8fd8-382bbfc53bdb"],

