 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"a5d693de-3014-4701-a3d8-99c712cf767e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9.4  Thermal-gradient fission: membrane-free division", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"ed6aaff8-47e1-4904-b2c4-7fb902a8ea26"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A temperature gradient makes the interaction ",
 StyleBox["\[Chi] ~ 1/T",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " position-dependent. A warm band (weakened cohesion) drawn through an \
elongated droplet dissolves its neck and splits it into two daughters \
\[LongDash] division without a membrane, a candidate protocell mechanism \
(Ianeselli 2022). The split is genuinely band-driven: two domains form with \
the band, only one without it."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dd0e5c51-086d-4457-8fc8-05e477dadc71"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"figThermalFission", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
