}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Figure 10.4  A protocell phylogeny generated by the same selection dynamics: \
fit (yellow) lineages branch and proliferate while low-fitness (blue) \
lineages die out (node colour = fitness).\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"2065d168-9712-4134-8196-bc135f6fa217"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["10.3  Reaction-diffusion inside condensates", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"ee56679c-f960-4adf-92dc-994e13235f35"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A condensate is also a chemical reactor. When crowding slows the activator \
far more than the inhibitor, the diffusion ratio ",
 StyleBox["D_v/D_u",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " crosses the ",
 StyleBox["Turing threshold",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " ",
 StyleBox["only inside",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " the dense phase: a band of wavenumbers becomes unstable there while every \
mode stays stable in the dilute surroundings, so spots self-organise inside \
the condensate and nowhere else. (The full 2D patterns, and the reaction \
hotspot that forms in a shell at the droplet interface, are computed in ",
 StyleBox["src/reaction_diffusion_cargo.py",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"22053618-7861-451e-b84a-d7849d66d7eb"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"figTuring", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  " In[34]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f007dd47-9fd9-447f-b0f7-b0e42d8ff14c"],

Cell[OutputFormData["\<\
Legended[-Graphics-, Placed[LineLegend[{Directive[Opacity[1.], 
 
>       AbsoluteThickness[2], RGBColor[0.78, 0.12, 0.36], Thickness[0.01]], 
 
>      Directive[Opacity[1.], AbsoluteThickness[2], 
 
>       RGBColor[0.12, 0.44, 0.7], Thickness[0.008], Dashing[{Small, \
Small}]]}
 
>      , {inside droplet (dense): unstable band, 
 
>      dilute phase: all modes stable}, LegendMarkers -> None, 
 
>     LabelStyle -> {}, LegendLayout -> Column], {0.62, 0.25}, Identity]]\
\>"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.991475171616315*^9},
 CellLabel->
  " Out[34]=",ExpressionUUID->"ff022afe-1716-43cf-bad2-5e76548ccb9c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Figure 10.5  Schnakenberg linear-stability growth rate ",
 StyleBox["\[Lambda](k)",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ": inside the dense phase a band of wavenumbers is unstable (patterns form), \
while in the dilute phase every mode is stable. The Turing instability is \
switched on by the condensate."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"1e4c0d92-239e-4440-896d-d96fb81feca8"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["10.4  Wet-dry cycling", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"51494d76-ef01-469c-a115-a22c8c2e8c96"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On the early Earth, rock pools cycled between flooded (wet) and evaporated \
(dry) states. Cycling the interaction ",
 StyleBox["\[Chi](t)=\[Chi]_0+\[CapitalDelta]\[Chi] sin(2\[Pi]t/T)",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " swings the system between a one-phase well (dissolve, remix) and a \
spinodally unstable double well (re-nucleate many droplets). Each dissolution \
erases the size differences that drive Ostwald ripening, so a ",
 StyleBox["population",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " of droplets is maintained, while a matched constant-",
 StyleBox["\[Chi]",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " run coarsens toward a single winner (Ianeselli 2022)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"30e21c11-228e-47a6-9bd8-3aed52127974"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"figWetDry", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  " In[35]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f0d876eb-a642-479f-baf2-003c868bec83"],

Cell[OutputFormData["\<\
Legended[-Graphics-, Placed[BarLegend[{Blend[RedBlueTones, #1] & , 
 
          69   69
>      {-(--), --}}, LabelStyle -> {}, LegendLayout -> Column, 
          50   50
 
>     LegendMarkerSize -> 408., ScalingFunctions -> {Identity, Identity}, 
 
>     Charting`AxisLabel -> None, Charting`TickSide -> Right, 
 
>     ColorFunctionScaling -> True], After, Identity]]\
\>"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.991475171912777*^9},
 CellLabel->
  " Out[35]=",ExpressionUUID->"6f808a81-5f92-4307-90ed-e0a7f54eb539"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Figure 10.6  1D wet\[Dash]dry Cahn\[Dash]Hilliard space\[Dash]time (",
 StyleBox["NDSolve",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "): with a cyclic well depth ",
 StyleBox["a(t)",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", domains dissolve at each wet half-cycle and re-nucleate at each dry \
half-cycle. The repeated dissolution resets the size differences that would \
otherwise drive Ostwald ripening, so a population of droplets is sustained \
rather than coarsening to a single winner (Ianeselli et al. 2022)."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"19c88255-354f-4b6f-9d61-e0bb9800947a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["10.5  The accessible parameter space", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"6e189455-6306-4fee-9bfd-87784c66fe78"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Finally, two analytic maps of the model's regimes: the ",
 StyleBox["(\[Chi],N)",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " plane separating one-phase from two-phase by the critical line ",
 StyleBox["\[Chi]_c(N)",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", and the ",
 StyleBox["(K,p)",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " mass-conserving rate-enhancement landscape with its optimal ridge ",
 StyleBox["p*\[TildeTilde]1/K",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ". (The full four-panel regime atlas \[LongDash] which also includes the \
thermodynamic ",
 StyleBox["(\[Phi]_0,\[Kappa])",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " plane and the active dissolution / microphase / macrophase plane from 2D \
simulations \[LongDash] is built in ",
 StyleBox["src/parameter_space.py",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f43f423c-1d2d-435f-b7d6-7e3ffc3543af"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"figParamSpace", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  " In[36]:=",ExpressionUUID->"13b477dc-4834-4596-acd6-1d5a4119345a"],

